{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfR8E6jBnwZbi3gBwA671","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `/app/answers.json` is written and valid. Summary of what I found:\n\n**q1 — matched-KL best-of-n: n = 41.**\nThe proposed PPO run (`kl=6.44235 steps=470`) actually reaches KL 2.738, not 6.44 — PPO approaches its target as `kl·(1−exp(−steps/849))`, which the notebook's own three PPO rows pin down exactly. Best-of-n follows `KL = ln n − (n−1)/n` (fits all four bon rows to 6 digits), and n = 41 gives KL 2.737962. The notes' \"n = 628\" used the wrong formula on the wrong KL.\n\n**q2 — length share of proxy reward: 0.392.**\nSweeping `len_pen` at six KL levels (96 train runs) shows proxy = 0.526·√KL + 0.56·tanh(Δlen/110), with Δlen = 304·√KL/(1+0.98·len_pen). Using noise-free modelled length, tanh fits at the seed-noise floor and every other saturating form fits ≥2× worse. At the recipe (Δlen ≈ 502, saturated) the length term is 0.560 of a 1.43 proxy → 39.2%.\n\n**q3 — pre-registered plan:** two gold runs at `gold_n=5450` each (cost 4360 ≤ 4400): `bon n=41` and the PPO recipe; rule `bon.gold_win_rate − ppo.gold_win_rate`, cuts >0.1 → bon, <−0.1 → ppo, else undetermined. Only gold win rate can separate worlds that differ in proxy/gold divergence; the budget's maximum gold_n gives σ≈0.009 on the difference. I validated the exact request format via `lab batch`: in this world it returns 0.555 − 0.323 = +0.23 → `bon`.\n\n**q4 — `bon_b`.** Gold at gold_n=2000: bon_b (n=60, len_pen=6.32) 0.763, ppo_ship 0.324, ppo_light 0.074, bon_a 0.033. The length the notes called \"quality\" is what the gold evaluator punishes; the length-penalised recipe wins by a wide margin.\n\nBudget used: ~9,240 of 20,000 GPU-hours."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":57321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_